%[text] %[text:anchor:H_2593FC52] ### **A Real Signal**
%[text] The pure 220 Hz note probably did not sound very appealing. Sounds generated by musical instruments tend to have several complementary frequencies (known as harmonics) that create a richer sound. Listen to the guitar note played below.
[yGuitar,FsGuitar] = audioread("Anote.mp3");
soundsc(yGuitar,FsGuitar)
%[text] You can analyze the guitar note in the time domain by plotting the audio signal. Below, about 10 milliseconds of the signal is plotted. 
tGuitar = (1:length(yGuitar))/FsGuitar; % Time variable
% Generate the plot
figure 
plot(tGuitar,yGuitar(:,1),"Linewidth",1)
xlim([0.1145 0.1245])
xlabel("t (s)")
ylabel("Amplitude")
